# Lab 07 -- Part 0: your personal test gateway + runner.
#
# Copy this file to .env (which is gitignored) and fill it in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Then bring the test pair up with:  ./scripts/setup.sh
# Always setup.sh on the FIRST run — it seeds the deploy API token into the
# test gateway's volume before its first boot. Later restarts may use plain
# `docker compose --profile test up -d`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONE value you must set. Lowercase, no spaces -- it becomes part of a
# GitHub runner label and a container name.
#
# Everything derives from it:
#   your runner's label     ->  <yourname>-local
#   your runner's name      ->  lab07-test-<yourname>
#   your workflow's runs-on ->  [self-hosted, <yourname>-local]   (Part 0 step 3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
LAB_USER=yourname

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your clone's scan-API key. Leave EMPTY: scripts/setup.sh (via
# scripts/generate-api-key.sh) generates `CICD-APIKEY:<secret>` here on first
# run and writes the hash-only token resource for your local gateway and your
# test gateway. docker-compose passes this value into your test-runner
# container, and your test-<yourname>.yml reads it from the runner's
# environment — no GitHub secret needed for your own gateway. (The repo's
# IGNITION_API_KEY Actions secret is production's key, minted by the
# instructors.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
IGNITION_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registering a runner on the shared repo needs repo-admin rights, which
# contributors do not have -- so the credential comes from Sam or Jasper.
#
#   RUNNER_TOKEN       what YOU use: the registration token posted in the
#                      Zoom chat at the start of Part 0. Valid 1 hour, can
#                      only enroll runners (it is not a login), and only has
#                      to work once: the registration persists in a volume.
#   RUNNER_GITHUB_PAT  instructor-only fallback for unattended machines --
#                      it carries repo-admin rights, so it is never handed
#                      out. The runner image prefers the PAT when both are
#                      set.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNNER_GITHUB_PAT=
RUNNER_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides -- only uncomment if you have a reason.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your runner's second label. Your test-<yourname>.yml's runs-on must match
# this EXACTLY, or your job waits forever for a runner that does not exist.
#RUNNER_LABEL=yourname-local

# What the runner is called under Settings -> Actions -> Runners.
#RUNNER_NAME=lab07-test-yourname

# Which repo the runner registers against.
#REPO_URL=https://github.com/Mustry-Academy/cicd-lab-07-multi-gateway-deploy
